==Description== <!--T:2-->

<!--T:3-->
When working with complex assemblies in FreeCAD, objects are often nested inside Part containers, link arrays, or linked across documents. Each nesting level applies its own placement transformation, making it difficult to determine the absolute (world) coordinates of a selected object.

This macro solves that problem by:

* Traversing the full hierarchy of containers, links, and link arrays
* Accumulating all placement transformations along the chain
* Displaying the final global placement (position, rotation, and scale) in the Report View
* Supporting link scales, which most other tools ignore

